 6.  **Define Splat Size:** Use the eigenvalues $\lambda_1$ and $\lambda_2$ to define the size (scale) of the splat along the tangent directions [S1, unofficial].
 
+**Pseudocode:**
+```python
+def compute_splat_orientation(points, centroid, kernel_radius):
+    # 1. Identify neighbors within kernel radius
+    neighbors = [p for p in points if distance(p, centroid) <= kernel_radius]
+    N = len(neighbors)
+    if N == 0:
+        return None, None, None, None, None, None
+
+    # 2. Compute local centroid
+    c_local = sum(neighbors) / N
+
+    # 3. Compute covariance matrix C
+    C = zeros((3, 3))
+    for p in neighbors:
+        diff = p - c_local
+        C += outer(diff, diff)
+    C = C / N
+
+    # 4. Solve eigenproblem
+    eigenvalues, eigenvectors = solve_eigenproblem(C)
+    # Sort by eigenvalue ascending: lambda_0 <= lambda_1 <= lambda_2
+    sorted_indices = argsort(eigenvalues)
+    lambda_0, lambda_1, lambda_2 = eigenvalues[sorted_indices]
+    v_0, v_1, v_2 = eigenvectors[:, sorted_indices]
+
+    # 5. Assign vectors
+    normal = v_0
+    tangent_1 = v_1
+    tangent_2 = v_2
+
+    # 6. Define size from eigenvalues
+    size_1 = sqrt(lambda_1)
+    size_2 = sqrt(lambda_2)
+
+    return normal, tangent_1, tangent_2, lambda_0, lambda_1, lambda_2
+```
